# Cloudflare Workers Assets header rules.
#
# Vite emits every JS/CSS asset under /assets/ with a content hash in the
# filename, so those files are immutable by construction: a change produces a
# new URL. Workers Assets defaults to `max-age=0, must-revalidate`, which made
# every returning visitor issue ~47 conditional requests (304s, ~23ms each)
# before the page could run.
#
# `immutable` tells the browser not to revalidate at all for a year. There is no
# consistency trade-off — the hash IS the invalidation strategy.
#
# NOTE: rules here APPEND to the platform default rather than replacing it, and
# a `/*` rule would append a second Cache-Control to every asset as well —
# producing `max-age=0, must-revalidate, public, max-age=31536000, immutable`,
# where browsers honour the FIRST max-age and the fix silently does nothing.
# So: set `! Cache-Control` to clear the inherited value first, and scope the
# rule to /assets/* only. Non-hashed files keep the platform default, which is
# what we want — they must revalidate or deploys would not be picked up.
/assets/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
